Title: The Korean War: Who Started It?

The Korean War, which lasted from to , was one of the bloodiest and most devastating conflicts of the 20th century. It involved the entire resources of both Koreas, as well as large numbers of troops and troops from the United States and China. The war began on June 25, , when North Korean forces, under Kim Il Sung, stormed across the 38th Parallel, a narrow demilitarized zone that separated the two Koreas.

The North Korean gamble was a success at first, as their forces swept southward, capturing Seoul within three days. But UN forces, led by General Douglas MacArthur, soon counterattacked and by mid-August pushed the North Koreans back across the border.

